	"_doc": "Story 020: battle backdrops drawn in code by BattleBackdrop (src/ui/battle_backdrop.gd), values from design/art-bible.md section 6. One entry per backdrop id: the 18 type ids (a fight in a zone uses the zone's gym type), 'route' (fallback for any unknown / empty id), 'league' (Conseil 4), 'ethernatos' (final boss), 'legendary' (legendary event fight). Fields: label (FR, QA only); sky [top, horizon]; ground [horizon, bottom] (one colour = bottom is that colour darkened by ground_darken); ground_detail none|stripes|tiles|waves|grass|cracks; glow (optional horizon glow colour); layers: list of silhouette layers drawn back to front {shape, count, height (px), alpha, color (optional; default = horizon sky colour darkened by far_darken for the first layer, ground colour darkened by near_darken for the others), base (fraction of the horizon height where the shapes stand, default 1.0), accent (optional second colour: lava, snow caps, windows, banners), seed}; particles (optional, <= 30) {color, count, size, vx, vy (px/s)}. Shapes: hills trees pines houses volcanoes peaks spikes rocks waves pylons pillars pipes dunes cactus clouds floating trunks webs cliffs tombs towers gears beams arches flowers banners rings crystals moon buildings. Story 020b: atmosphere (optional) = parameters of the painted-look shader layer src/ui/shaders/backdrop_atmosphere.gdshader drawn over the code backdrop: {fog (haze colour), fog_density 0..1 (horizon haze + ground mist), glow_color, glow 0..1 (horizon light), rays 0..1 (light shafts from the sun), sun_x 0..1 (sun position), clouds 0..1 (soft noise clouds)}; each layer also fades into the fog at its base (atmospheric perspective, haze_far / haze_near). painted_path: if that image exists (any extension of painted_extensions, png first) for a backdrop id it is drawn full-screen instead of the code backdrop (prompts: design/art/backdrop-prompts.md); painted_fog_scale / painted_platform_alpha soften the shader and platforms over it.",
